# ALL.mask -- R-409 line masks for icon_lab (entry<TAB>L<n>-or-python-regex<TAB>reason); the same rules on the oracle's stream and on SCRIP's, a masked line replaced by its marker and never deleted.
lab1/p1	L3	&clock of p1.icn (write(&clock)), the time of day: a machine or system value, masked on both sides and never excluded (Lon 2026-11-17: "remember the masking of machine/system specific is how a test passes."); MEASURED: iconx run twice a second apart differs on line 3 alone
lab1/p1	L5	&date of p1.icn (write(&date)), the date of the run: a machine or system value, masked on both sides and never excluded (Lon 2026-11-17: "remember the masking of machine/system specific is how a test passes."); MEASURED: iconx run twice a second apart differs on line 3 alone
lab1/p1	L6	&dateline of p1.icn (write(&dateline)), the date and time of the run in words: a machine or system value, masked on both sides and never excluded (Lon 2026-11-17: "remember the masking of machine/system specific is how a test passes."); MEASURED: iconx run twice a second apart differs on line 3 alone
lab1/p1	L7	&time of p1.icn (write(&time)), the milliseconds of CPU used, 4 on SCRIP and 0 on the oracle (the runtime's own): a machine or system value, masked on both sides and never excluded (Lon 2026-11-17: "remember the masking of machine/system specific is how a test passes."); MEASURED: iconx run twice a second apart differs on line 3 alone
lab1/p1	L8	&host of p1.icn (write(&host)), the name of the machine: a machine or system value, masked on both sides and never excluded (Lon 2026-11-17: "remember the masking of machine/system specific is how a test passes."); MEASURED: iconx run twice a second apart differs on line 3 alone
